  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nSkies remained cloudy much of the day, limiting mixing and\ndrying at the surface. Clouds will continue to clear this\nevening, with radiational cooling. This could result in patchy\nfog developing across the area, with some pockets of freezing\nfog also possible as surface temperatures drop below freezing. A\nSpecial Weather Statement was issued to highlight this\npotential, and will monitor future trends for any advisory that\nmay be needed.\n\nDry conditions continue through the upcoming week as mid-level \nridging builds across the eastern CONUS. Surface high pressure \nis nudging its way into the region from the west and subsidence \neating away clouds across Ohio can be observed on satellite \nimagery. \n\nEnsemble mean PWATs tank to below a quarter inch or less \nthrough the upcoming week. Rising heights work to gradually \nmoderate temperatures through the week. Widespread low 50s \nreturn by Tuesday and then probabilities of >60 degree high \ntemperatures rise to ~20% by Wednesday and then jump as high as \n60-90% Wednesday through the latter part of the work week. \n\nSkies have been slow to clear this morning with moisture \ntrapped underneath the subsidence inversion but largely \ncloudless skies are favored through the week. Clear skies and \nlight winds under surface high pressure promote efficient \nradiative cooling nodding towards large diurnal swings (some \nnighttime lows in the upper 20s) and a chance for fog \ndevelopment, especially along area rivers. \n\nOur next chance for rain looks quite far off tied to a possible\ntrough swinging through the central CONUS and then Ohio Valley \nnear the end of the upcoming weekend. Despite some ensemble \nagreement on an arrival on Sunday, clustered ensembles paint a \nfar less clear picture with varying degrees of ridging or \ntroughing for the late weekend. Much of the uncertainty in \ntiming looks tied to smaller waves building through the flow \naround Friday. At this time, a high confidence period of dry \nweather is expected through the end of the work week and \npossibly into the weekend, with solutions diverging thereafter.",
